{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00427","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00427@rel:R25-11#1ff272ae","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00427","release":"R25-11","content":"function RecoverKey [SWS_PER_00427] Upstream: RS_PER_00003 , RS_PER_00009 , RS_PER_00010 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_AP_00121 , RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00128 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; RecoverKey ( ara::core::StringView key) noexcept; Recovers a single key-value pair of this Key Value Storage. This method allows to recover a single key-value pair when the redundancy checks fail. This method does a best-effort recovery of the key-value pair. After recovery, the key-value pair might contain outdated or initial content, or might be lost. RecoverKey may be delayed by an ongoing call from another thread to RemoveAllKeys, SyncTo Storage, or DiscardPendingChanges, or to SetValue, GetValue, GetCurrentValueSize, Remove Key, RecoverKey, or ResetKey for the same key-value pair. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/key_value_storage.h\" class mono Scope class ara::per::KeyValueStorage class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe PerErrc ::kKeyNotFound rollback_semantics class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td key td The key to be recovered. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; td A Result of void. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td Returned if the provided key does not exist in the Key-Value td Storage. td td PerErrc ::kIllegalWriteAccess td rollback_semantics Returned if the Key-Value Storage is configured as read- only. td PerErrc ::kPhysicalStorageFailure td no_rollback_semantics Returned if access to the physical storage fails. td PerErrc ::kIntegrityCorrupted td rollback_semantics Returned if stored data cannot be written because the structural integrity is corrupted. td PerErrc ::kEncryptionFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the encryption or decryption of stored data fails. td PerErrc ::kOutOfStorageSpace td no_rollback_semantics Returned if the available physical storage space is insufficient for the recovered value. td PerErrc ::kQuotaExceeded td rollback_semantics Returned if the recovered value would exceed the configured maximumAllowedSize of the Key-Value Storage. td PerErrc ::kAuthenticationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if calculating or checking the MAC of stored data fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00427","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11"],"platform_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11"},"element":{"kind":"function","name":"RecoverKey","module":"PER","cluster":"","page":"classes/cl_ara_per_KeyValueStorage_e55123.html","doc_type":"SWS","ai":false,"first":"R25-11","last":"R25-11","changed":[],"distinct":1},"evidence":{"figures":[{"id":"FIG-b045d30e3c97fa76","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_EXP_SWArchitecture","p":90,"rel":[],"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"RecoverKey API in KeyValueStorage","n":16,"cap":"Figure 9.36: Interfaces for key-value-based data storage","sha":"b045d30e3c97fa76804aee0624930cbac3f6a04b3d15be2ecbb043d7043e46b6","nser":5,"src":"figure"},{"id":"FIG-67a0c9934f8b513a","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_EXP_SWArchitecture","p":55,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.9,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"KeyValueStorage RecoverKey method","n":14,"cap":"Figure 9.14: Interfaces required by State Management","sha":"67a0c9934f8b513aa4eccf85c17d21fac9083c5e1911afb304b3e862fabd997a","